{'symbol': 'ORCL', 'date': '2023-05-10 12:30:00', 'title': 'ORACLE NAMED A LEADER IN THE 2023 GARTNER® MAGIC QUADRANT™ FOR WAREHOUSE MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS', 'text': 'ORACLE POSITIONED AS A LEADER BASED ON "ABILITY TO EXECUTE" AND "COMPLETENESS OF VISION" AUSTIN, TEXAS , MAY 10, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0ORACLE HAS BEEN NAMED A LEADER IN THE 2023 GARTNER MAGIC QUADRANT FOR WAREHOUSE MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS (WMS) FOR ORACLE FUSION CLOUD WAREHOUSE MANAGEMENT\xa0FOR THE EIGHTH CONSECUTIVE YEAR. THE MAGIC QUADRANT, WHICH EVALUATED 18 COMPANIES,\xa0RECOGNIZED ORACLE AS A LEADER BASED ON "COMPLETENESS OF VISION" AND "ABILITY TO EXECUTE".'}{'symbol': 'ORCL', 'date': '2023-05-10 09:00:00', 'title': 'STUDY: 77% OF U.S. EMPLOYEES FEEL LIKE THEY ARE JUST A COG IN A CORPORATE MACHINE', 'text': "52% ARE MORE WORRIED ABOUT HAVING THE RIGHT JOB THAN THE RIGHT SALARY 88% WOULD WALK AWAY FROM A JOB THAT DOESN'T MEET THEIR EXPECTATIONS, EVEN DURING A RECESSION 85% OF HR LEADERS KNOW A POOR EMPLOYEE EXPERIENCE CAN HAVE SERIOUS BUSINESS CONSEQUENCES AUSTIN, TEXAS , MAY 10, 2023 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- HR LEADERS ARE STRUGGLING TO KEEP UP WITH CHANGING EMPLOYEE EXPECTATIONS, AND THIS CAN HAVE DIRE CONSEQUENCES FOR BUSINESSES, ACCORDING TO A NEW STUDY\xa0BY ORACLE. THE SURVEY OF 1,000 EMPLOYEES AND HR LEADERS ACROSS THE UNITED STATES (U.S.) FOUND THAT DESPITE CURRENT ECONOMIC UNCERTAINTY, WORKER EXPECTATIONS ARE HIGHER THAN EVER, AND HR LEADERS NEED HELP TO GET THE EMPLOYEE EXPERIENCE RIGHT OR RISK LOSING PROFITS AND MARKET SHARE."}